    requirement;
(c) you must retain the original copyright notice, author attribution,
    project name, and repository link;
(d) you must clearly state that changes were made, and provide a reasonable
    summary of the modifications;
(e) you must not misrepresent the Modified Version as the original Work;
(f) if binaries, JAR files, packaged releases, or other compiled forms are
    distributed, the full corresponding source code must be made available in a
    convenient and publicly accessible form at no additional charge.

For clarity, private modifications that are not Distributed to any third party
do not trigger the source distribution requirement under this Section 4.

5. No Closed Redistribution of Derivatives

You may not Distribute any Modified Version in binary-only, JAR-only,
obfuscated-only, or source-withheld form.

Any Distributed Modified Version must include or be accompanied by complete
corresponding source code under this same License.

6. Attribution

Any Distribution of the Work or a Modified Version must preserve:

- the project name identified above;
- the author name "Ice2974" unless otherwise explicitly stated by the copyright
